{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling for every lane: one START and one END act cover a run of short\nunits.\n\nIdentifiers (b) filed six acts in 15 minutes for three short steps: the\nworking checks, the vector producer and one AST value. Each act costs a\nfiling and a read. The slot acts exist so that two actors never run\nheavy work together, and so that I deploy in a free window.\n\nFrom now on:\n\n- A unit that runs no test, no gate and no control, and that ends in\n  under five minutes, needs no act of its own. File one START before\n  the first such unit and one END after the last. The END lists each\n  unit, its actual exit and its evidence path.\n- A sealed focus unit, a gate and a controls unit keep their own START\n  and END acts.\n- A correction of a digest goes in the next act that you file anyway,\n  unless a reviewer already rests on the wrong value.\n\nThe evidence rules do not change. Ruling 7e5c79f2 stands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}